  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1402.06 Materials Derived from Used Oil",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1402.06 Materials Derived from Used Oil.\n\n(a) Materials, including re-refined lubricants, that are reclaimed from used oil, are used beneficially, and are not burned for energy recovery or used in a manner constituting disposal, shall be subject to Env-Hw 401.03(b)(39).\n\n(b) Materials produced from used oil that are burned for energy recovery, such as used oil fuels, shall be subject to regulation as used oil under this chapter.\n\n(c) Materials derived from used oil that are disposed of or used in a manner constituting disposal shall be subject to the applicable requirements of Env-Hw 100 through Env-Hw 800 and Env-Hw 1200 including the applicable requirements of Env-Hw 401.03(b)(26), rather than this chapter.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
